{"filetype":"text/html","chroma:document":"LIFO: Never replace the seed set of examples and only the last one gets replaced with the latest successful attacks. But quite limited in terms of diversity and attack effectiveness.\n\nScoring: Essentially this is a priority queue where examples are ranked by scores. Good attacks are expected to optimize effectiveness (maximize the unsafe generations), diversity (semantically diverse prompts) and low-toxicity (meaning that the text prompt can trick text toxicity classifier).\n\nEffectiveness is measured by attack objective functions designed for different experiments: - In text-to-image experiment, they used Q16 (Schramowski et al. 2022) and NudeNet (https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet). - text-to-text experiment: TOXIGEN\n\nDiversity is measured by pairwise dissimilarity, in form of $\\sum_{(\\mathbf{x}_i, \\mathbf{x}_j) \\in \\text{All pairs}} [1 - \\text{sim}(\\mathbf{x}_i, \\mathbf{x}_j)]$\n\nLow-toxicity is measured by Perspective API.","orig_elements":"","emphasized_text_contents":["black box","What","NOUN","→Which","NOUN","WP","is →","WP","’s’","was→is","GBDA","make adversarial loss optimization differentiable","extreme","“a similarity score for evaluating text generation that captures the semantic similarity between pairwise tokens in contextualized embeddings of a transformer model.”","HotFlip","Universal Adversarial Triggers","UAT","AutoPrompt","UAT-LM","UTSC","unigram","affirmative","greedy coordinate gradient (GCG)","transferability","ARCA","coordinate ascent","should have been mitigated","Competing objective","Mismatched generalization","Display of saliency score of each token","Token substitution and insertion","Zero-shot generation","Stochastic few-shot generation","Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Explore","Establish","Exploit","FLIRT","update in-context exemplars","FIFO","LIFO","the last one","Scoring","effectiveness","diversity","low-toxicity","Scoring-LIFO","robust","inner maximization","outer minimization","Inner maximization","Outer minimization","instruct","adversarial training","Paraphrase","Retokenization"],"url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-10-25-adv-attack-llm/","category":"CompositeElement","emphasized_text_tags":["b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","b","b","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i"],"element_id":"2775507ceeaaa257529304164be2b816","link_texts":["#","Morris et al. 2020","Ribeiro et al (2018)","EDA","Wei & Zou 2019","Jin et al. 2019","Li et al. 2020","#","Guo et al. 2021","Jang et al. 2016","Zhang et al. 2019","Ebrahimi et al. 2018","Wallace et al. (2019)","HotFlip","Shin et al., 2020","Mehrabi et al. (2022)","Zou et al. (2023)","OpenAI 2023","UAT and AutoPrompt","Jones et al. 2023","#","Wei et al. (2023)","DAN","AIM","it can understand","Wei et al. (2023)","Greshake et al. (2023)","#","Wallace et al. (2019)","QuizBowl QA dataset","Ziegler et al. (2022)","Wallace et al. (2019)","BERT-Attack","Xu et al. 2021","BAD dataset","Tensorflow dataset","red-teaming dataset","Ganguli, et al. 2022","GPT-4","DALL-E 3","#","Perez et al. 2022","A2C","BAD (Bot Adversarial Dialogue) dataset","nucleus sampling","Casper et al. (2023)","Perez et al. (2022)","here","here","here","Mehrabi et al. 2023","in-context learning","Perez et al. 2022","Schramowski et al. 2022","https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet)","Perspective API","#","#","Madry et al. 2017","#","Xie et al. 2023","Jain et al. 2023","White-box attacks","UAT-LM","Jain et al. 2023","#","#","“Towards Deep Learning Models Resistant to Adversarial Attacks”","“Semantically equivalent adversarial rules for debugging NLP models”","“Gradient-based adversarial attacks against text transformers”","“HotFlip: White-Box Adversarial Examples for Text Classification”","“Universal Adversarial Triggers for Attacking and Analyzing NLP.”","code","“Robust Co